### English: talking to people at their doors (the talk panel): who they are,
### what they say when a quest can't be taken yet, and when something asked
### can't be done. Hints are in the giver's words, never numbers (owner).

## Who someone is, as the talk panel's title: "Mara Tull, baker".

giver-title = { $name }, { $occupation }

## What the giver of each kind of building does (a house's has none).

occupation-shrine = keeper of the shrine
occupation-inn = innkeeper
occupation-tavern = tavern keeper
occupation-blacksmith = blacksmith
occupation-herbalist = herbalist
occupation-carpenter = carpenter
occupation-tailor = tailor
occupation-leatherworker = leatherworker
occupation-fletcher = fletcher
occupation-church = priest
occupation-weaponsmith = weaponsmith
occupation-armoursmith = armoursmith
occupation-potion-shop = apothecary
occupation-training-hall = trainer
occupation-scroll-shop = scribe
occupation-adventurers-guild = guildmaster
occupation-jeweller = jeweller
occupation-library = librarian
occupation-bank = banker
occupation-gem-cutter = gem cutter
occupation-black-market = fence
occupation-cathedral = bishop

## What the panel says with nothing to offer.

talk-nothing = I've nothing for you just now.

## Why a quest can't be taken yet ("!" in grey), in the giver's words.

hint-standing-known = Folk round here don't know you yet.
hint-standing-trusted = I'd want to know you better before I ask this.
hint-standing-honoured = This is for someone the town holds in honour.
hint-standing-champion = Only the town's own champion could help me with this.
hint-earlier = Help me with what I've already asked first.
hint-elsewhere-named = They speak of you in { $town }? Not yet, they don't.
hint-elsewhere = Someone else should have good words for you first.
hint-skill = I'd want someone good at { $skill }.
hint-dealt-with = I've heard what you did out there. I won't forget it.
hint-found = I've heard you came across something of ours. Hold on to it.

## When something asked of a quest can't be done.

refused-too-many = You've taken on too much here already: finish or give up some of it first.
refused-no-room = You can't carry it all. I'll keep it for you until you can.
refused-not-offered = That isn't mine to give you now.
refused-not-ready = That isn't done yet.

## Above the reward, and the giver's words at the end.

talk-reward = Reward: { $reward }
talk-steps = What to do:
talk-dealt-with = "I've already dealt with it," you tell them. "Then the worst of it is done."
talk-found = "I've already found it," you tell them. "Then you've saved me a long walk."
talk-step-done = { $step } (done)

## The button going into a quest's own dungeon by the giver's door.

talk-enter-cellar = Enter Cellar
